cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite them as below, and cite the accompanying methods report."
title: "Synthyrion proofs: bounded-proof results, timing-analysis tables and the proof engine"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Synthyrion-Systems-and-Technologies/synthyrion-proofs"
url: "https://synthyrion.com"
abstract: "Results, checker outputs and a runnable bounded proof engine behind the Synthyrion Core L5 kernel: the panic-freedom census of 5,659 kernel decision functions, the worst-case-timing registry of 140 kernel entry points with its tables, the bounded-proof statements with their domains and outcomes, SHA-512 fingerprints of the checker outputs, and the proof engine with a small subject. The repository contains no kernel source."
keywords:
  - microkernel
  - Rust
  - bounded proof
  - exhaustive checking
  - worst-case execution time
  - verification methods
